{
  "protocol": 1,
  "about": "Contract examples for the Scouty LinkedIn capture protocol, version 1. Committed byte-identical in scouty (src/lib/linkedin/__fixtures__/protocol-v1) and scouty-ext (protocol-v1). All content is synthetic.",
  "rules": [
    "Every file is UTF-8 JSON, two-space indented, with one trailing newline. valid/section-*.json are exact request bodies: the Content-Digest of each is the sha256 recorded for it in valid/manifest-complete.json (hex there, base64 in the header).",
    "Profile kinds (profile, experience, skills): profile is an object, blocks is [], blockCount equals profile.sections.length. Activity kinds (posts, comments, reactions): profile is null, blockCount equals blocks.length.",
    "Lengths are counted in Unicode code points. name is at most 300 and headline at most 500 on the wire.",
    "invalid/*.json wrap the body: { note, kind: section | manifest | create, pathSection, expect: { status, code }, body }.",
    "responses/*.json are example response bodies. Counts are { profileSections, posts, comments, reactions }."
  ],
